actly like ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled"},{"type":"text","text":"] (D-20): a tenant"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"may turn its organization’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" off and never its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" on. * ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::ssf_enabled"},{"type":"text","text":"],"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"validated "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"disable-only"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the same way (D-45). * ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dynamic_registration"},{"type":"text","text":"], on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ladder "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"disabled"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"initial_access_token"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymous"},{"type":"text","text":": a tenant may move down it and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never up. * ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_max_clients"},{"type":"text","text":"] and ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_unused_client_ttl_days"},{"type":"text","text":"], on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ordinary "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tenant <= org"},{"type":"text","text":" rule — with the wrinkle that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":" on the second means "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"never sweep","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is the longest window of all and is handled by ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dcr_ttl_strictness"},{"type":"text","text":"]. "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ordered","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", therefore never validated against the baseline and never clamped: *"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::default_locale"},{"type":"text","text":"]. A language is a presentation preference; there is no sense in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which Italian is stricter than French. * ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_allowed_scopes"},{"type":"text","text":"],"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts"},{"type":"text","text":"] and ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::external_client_allowed_resources"},{"type":"text","text":"]. Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names per-tenant resources — "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" tenant’s MCP servers, "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" tenant’s callback hosts —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and there is no sense in which one such list is stricter than another. A subset rule would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"force an organization to enumerate every tenant’s resource servers in its own baseline"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before any tenant could name one. The model’s rule is “a tenant may only be more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"restrictive”, which binds every field that "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"has"}]},{"type":"text","text":" a restrictiveness; a field that has none"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cannot violate it. One cross-field interlock spans both groups and is checked on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resolved policy rather than on either input: see ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"validate_dcr_policy"},{"type":"text","text":"]."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/Axi